          "path": "_m/g/c/n/2/dorset-museum-wp/fordington-mosaic-dorchester.jpg",
          "filename": "Fordington Mosaic - Dorchester.jpg",
          "caption": "Roman Mosaic Pavement of 4th century date, found in 1903 on the site of Lott and Walnes's Foundary, High Street, Fordington, and lifted in 1927. The head in the apse is of Oceanus flanked by two dolphins and two fish. The god's hair and beard are seaweed. The work is similar to that of the Neptune mosaic at Frampton, and may have been designed and made by the Dorchester School of Mosaicists. On display in the Dorset County Museum.",
          "alt": "Roman Mosaic Pavement of 4th century date, found in 1903 on the site of Lott and Walnes's Foundary, High Street, Fordington, and lifted in 1927. The head in the apse is of Oceanus flanked by two dolphins and two fish. The god's hair and beard are seaweed. The work is similar to that of the Neptune mosaic at Frampton, and may have been designed and made by the Dorchester School of Mosaicists. On display in the Dorset County Museum.",
